WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.876
Hi, I'm Bowline!

00:00:02.876 --> 00:00:05.595
Kimi K3.1 Pro is Moonshot's new flagship.

00:00:05.595 --> 00:00:08.703
The surprise is what didn't change: the network.

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:13.520
K3.1 Pro is a post-trained version of K3.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.054
Same experts, same attention, same window.

00:00:16.054 --> 00:00:20.276
The gains came from a much bigger reinforcement learning budget.

00:00:21.758 --> 00:00:23.322
Start from the K3 checkpoint.

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:25.198
The policy keeps the same shape.

00:00:25.618 --> 00:00:30.346
Most of the cost is generation: long agent runs against tools, in

00:00:30.346 --> 00:00:32.316
sandboxes across hundreds of domains.

00:00:32.736 --> 00:00:34.721
Every domain has its own reward.

00:00:34.721 --> 00:00:38.692
One buggy environment can teach the wrong thing, so Moonshot vets them

00:00:38.692 --> 00:00:40.016
on a shared platform.

00:00:40.436 --> 00:00:42.176
Then update, and around again.

00:00:42.176 --> 00:00:45.655
The claim is that extra compute now pays off predictably.

00:00:47.317 --> 00:00:51.320
K3 trained nine separate experts, then distilled them into one model.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:57.234
K3.1 Pro runs joint reinforcement learning across hundreds of domains, and strips

00:00:57.234 --> 00:00:59.523
cyber data, even from mid-training.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.338
Moonshot hasn't said how Highspeed is faster.

00:01:03.338 --> 00:01:05.428
This is my reasoning, not theirs.

00:01:05.848 --> 00:01:08.793
Both endpoints list the same model and the same precision.

00:01:09.213 --> 00:01:12.592
Serve fewer users per copy, and each user's step gets shorter.

00:01:13.012 --> 00:01:15.513
Or draft more tokens ahead, and discard more.

00:01:15.933 --> 00:01:18.647
Either way, each token costs more GPU time.

00:01:18.647 --> 00:01:20.343
That fits a doubled price.

00:01:21.758 --> 00:01:27.072
On Terminal-Bench four point oh, K3.1 Pro nearly ties Claude Opus five point five.

00:01:27.492 --> 00:01:32.063
It leads on agentic, tool-using work like OfficeQA Pro, and trails on

00:01:32.063 --> 00:01:33.587
closed-book knowledge and cyber.

00:01:35.092 --> 00:01:40.208
The sixty-five percent drop is this internal stress test, checked claim by claim.

00:01:40.208 --> 00:01:42.176
GPT-6 Astra is still lower.

00:01:43.683 --> 00:01:48.224
The lesson: a new flagship can be the same network, trained much harder afterwards.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:54.750
Same shape, more reinforcement learning, a lead on agentic work, and

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.150
weights promised for November.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:58.688
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:58.688 --> 00:01:59.293
I'm Bowline.

00:01:59.293 --> 00:01:59.596
Bye!
